<title>SINGAPORE: Keppel out of S$300 mln Filipino deal - TV.</title>
<headline>Keppel out of S$300 mln Filipino deal - TV.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Conglomerate Keppel Corp Ltd on Tuesday pulled out of a potential Singapore $300 million deal to buy a controlling stake in a Philippines food processing plant, Singapore state television said.</p>
<p>Keppel pulled out of the deal to buy 51 percent of Food Terminal Inc after it re- examined the project's feasibility, the report said.</p>
<p>Keppel and a consortium of companies including SM Investment Corp, had pre- qualified to bid for a 51 percent stake in the food processing plant based south of Manila.</p>
<p>Bidding for the plant is due to take place on Wednesday.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703011)</p>
